# RELEASE — Zypper-Package-History-Logs

Version:  v4.2
Date:     2026-04-04
Platform: openSUSE Tumbleweed
Script:   /usr/local/bin/zypper-history

---

## What's in this release

### New features
- Interactive listing of all days with recorded zypper activity — shows package and command counts per day
- Dynamic repository color assignment at runtime via `zypper repos` — works with any user repository configuration, no hardcoded repo names

### Output
- Full ANSI color support — install (green), remove (red), per-repository colors
- Paginated output via `less -R` — navigable history for long logs
- CSV export to `~/Audits/` with restricted permissions (600)

### Reliability
- `set -euo pipefail` — strict error handling, fails fast on unexpected input
- Safe IFS — protects against word splitting in package names
- Strict date validation: format check, calendar bounds, future date rejection
- Root check with interactive sudo fallback

### Interface
- `-h` / `--help` — usage and examples
- `-v` / `--version` — displays current version
- Multi-language message system (French)

---

## Usage

```bash
# Install
sudo cp zypper-history /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/zypper-history

# Show history for a specific date
sudo zypper-history 2026-04-04

# List all days with activity
sudo zypper-history --list
```
